------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pyyaml = Read & Write YAML files from Python! // pyyaml = Read & Write YAML config files from Python!
Since YAML is used EVERYWHERE in DevOps — Kubernetes, Docker, CI/CD — this library is essential! 🚀
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
📊 Summary Table

Task                     | Code
-------------------------|-----------------------------------
Read YAML file           | yaml.safe_load(file)

Write YAML file          | yaml.dump(data, file)

YAML string to Python    | yaml.safe_load(string)

Python to YAML string    | yaml.dump(data)

Read multiple docs       | yaml.safe_load_all(file)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🤔 First – What is YAML?

# YAML is a config file format used everywhere in DevOps

name: myapp
version: 1.0
environment: production
port: 8080

database:
  host: localhost
  port: 5432
  name: mydb

servers:
  - web1
  - web2
  - web3

YAML is used in:

✅ Kubernetes   → deployment.yaml
✅ Docker       → docker-compose.yaml
✅ GitHub Actions → .github/workflows/ci.yaml
✅ Ansible      → playbook.yaml
✅ Helm Charts  → values.yaml
✅ ArgoCD       → application.yaml
